# Negative-control mutant — a list row's price follows the portal brand's tax type (B4)
#
# Scenario it must flip: a list spec that serves `brand/settings` with
#   `tax_type: 0` (EXCLUDE_TAX) and asserts each row's `priceFormatted` is its
#   net figure (`configuration_total_recurring_net_amount_formatted` for a
#   subscription, `configuration_net_amount_discounted_formatted` for a
#   one-time product) over a capture whose net and gross figures differ. A
#   list row carries no `brand`, so the portal brand's tax type is the only
#   source.
# Mutation: the price ignores the portal brand's `taxType` and reads the
#   record's own brand only, so every list row shows its tax-inclusive price.
